{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.ArchimedeanRemainderExponentialDecay","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.ArchimedeanRemainderExponentialDecay","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ArchimedeanRemainderExponentialDecay.exp_decay_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ArchimedeanRemainderExponentialDecay.exp_decay_bound","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/archimedean-remainder-exponential-decay.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Exponential-decay control of the truncation remainder: there is a\npositive prefactor `C` and positive rate `c` with\n`|remainder N| ≤ C · exp(−c · N)` for every truncation depth `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ArchimedeanRemainderExponentialDecay.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ArchimedeanRemainderExponentialDecay.mk","kind":"ctor","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/archimedean-remainder-exponential-decay.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ArchimedeanRemainderExponentialDecay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ArchimedeanRemainderExponentialDecay","kind":"class","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/archimedean-remainder-exponential-decay.lean#L38-L60","doc":"**Primary conjecture (archimedean remainder exponential decay).**\n\nCarrier class axiomatising the open input.  The single field encodes\nthe conjecture's content in the *shape* of the claim: for the chosen\nfree-neutron sector there exist a strictly positive prefactor `C` and\na strictly positive rate `c` controlling the truncation remainder\n`remainder : ℕ → ℝ` (the map `N ↦ R_N(K)`) by `C · exp(−c · N)` at\nevery depth `N`.\n\nThis is **not** a vacuous marker: discharging it requires producing\nthe two positive constants and proving the `∀ N` exponential bound on\nthe actual remainder function — exactly the open spectral-tail\nestimate.  No instance is provided here, faithfully representing the\nconjecture's open state. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:archimedean-remainder-exponential-decay","label":"conj:archimedean-remainder-exponential-decay","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/archimedean-remainder-exponential-decay.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}